{"title":"1998 AJHSME Problems/Problem 19","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Tamika selects two different numbers at random from the set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/1/63100050d75fe3497e57190e12f7679eb69ca95c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{ 8,9,10 \\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"69\" height=\"18\" /> and adds them.  Carlos takes two different numbers at random from the set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/4/e143cac2b32c71aeb760da87e92a1b24e32dbf1b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{3, 5, 6\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"60\" height=\"18\" /> and multiplies them.  What is the probability that Tamika's result is greater than Carlos' result?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/1/761d2e44b7c3bfc22d2953b42ac263dda94deb2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A)}\\ \\dfrac{4}{9} \\qquad \\text{(B)}\\ \\dfrac{5}{9} \\qquad \\text{(C)}\\ \\dfrac{1}{2} \\qquad \\text{(D)}\\ \\dfrac{1}{3} \\qquad \\text{(E)}\\ \\dfrac{2}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"349\" height=\"37\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The different possible (and equally likely) values Tamika gets are:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/3/e932d5e25ecbcfc490ebca3571147cde2874f7c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8+9=17$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"82\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/c/3ac7de26fc4a1b4cc8e5f703c77c4bc8cec70b89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8+10=18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"91\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/a/20a1376fe63a8c335d341067d6788d6bb2cd3a8c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9+10=19$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"91\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>The different possible (and equally likely) values Carlos gets are:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/f/59fcfa0437fb6df2d998017e53ab6ad86ce473df.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3\\times5=15$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"82\" height=\"13\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/1/b11b22377402b1d083abd2dfc7369887fb5c0719.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3\\times6=18$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"82\" height=\"13\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/a/2ca119c583bd80fa32281ef38796942203098d0f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5\\times6=30$\" width=\"82\" height=\"12\" />\n</p><p>The probability that if Tamika had the sum <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/6/b7616a230c77f0d9a577e5bca01aa06f1c35c457.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$17$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> her sum would be greater than Carlos's set is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/1/4e1965f8d70832ded66434c75a7bd52b75090af0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" />, because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/6/b7616a230c77f0d9a577e5bca01aa06f1c35c457.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$17$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> is only greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/9/f1965fae079a9ba2c0726c307070c2355dfcb213.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>The probability that if Tamika had the sum <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/7/5e7a1b6098a8c98b8e4adae526aeef4b91712620.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> her sum would be greater than Carlos's set is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/1/4e1965f8d70832ded66434c75a7bd52b75090af0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" />, because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/7/5e7a1b6098a8c98b8e4adae526aeef4b91712620.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> is only greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/9/f1965fae079a9ba2c0726c307070c2355dfcb213.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>The probability that if Tamika had the sum <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/b/efbfe273946ff9f971c5eab331ca39caa6fdf7f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$19$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> her sum would be greater than Carlos's set is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/4/7547747b133453d3c209cff6cfbf129aa67a6947.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" />, because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/b/efbfe273946ff9f971c5eab331ca39caa6fdf7f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$19$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> is greater than both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/9/f1965fae079a9ba2c0726c307070c2355dfcb213.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/7/5e7a1b6098a8c98b8e4adae526aeef4b91712620.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>Each sum has a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/1/4e1965f8d70832ded66434c75a7bd52b75090af0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> possibility of being chosen, so we have\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/3/533e1279067e1eca5a8881b957eb0b9e26791d4d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{3}\\left(\\frac{1}{3}+\\frac{1}{3}+\\frac{2}{3}\\right)=\\frac{1}{3}\\left(\\frac{4}{3}\\right)=\\frac{4}{9}=\\boxed{A}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"292\" height=\"43\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_AJHSME\" title=\"1998 AJHSME\">1998 AJHSME</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_AJHSME_Problems\" title=\"1998 AJHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_AJHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1998 AJHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=42&amp;year=1998\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"1998 AJHSME Problems/Problem 18\">Problem 18</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"1998 AJHSME Problems/Problem 20\">Problem 20</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\